FUNDAMENTALS
A magic square of order n is an n×n array of distinct numbers
such that every row, every column and both main diagonals
sum to the same constant S.

This square additionally satisfies:
- every 2×2 block sums to 139
- both broken diagonals (wrap-around) sum to 139
- four corners sum to 139
- any pair of numbers diametrically opposite through the
  center sums to 139/2 wait no — opposite pairs sum to 34? 
